Q:
Find the following limit using either forms or continuity: lim as x -> infinity of (e^x+e^(-x))/(e^x-e^(-x))

A:
1

e^x grows while e^(-x) decays as x -> infinity.

lim as x -> infinity of (e^x+e^(-x))/(e^x-e^(-x)) ~ lim as x -> infinity of e^x/e^x

lim as x -> infinity of e^x/e^x = lim as x -> infinity of 1 = 1

Thus lim as x -> infinity of (e^x+e^(-x))/(e^x-e^(-x)) = 1

